  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A thin prism of angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;made of glass of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;is combined with another prism of glass of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn></math>. The combination of the prisms produces dispersion without deviation. The angle of the second prism should be</p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
